    <bpmn:process id="W_W5556" name="W5556. Product-Tampering Threat, Extortion Demand &amp; Merchandise-Integrity Sweep Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: A threat, extortion demand, or malicious claim that BuildRight merchandise on shelves has been or will be contaminated, tampered with, or booby-trapped — by call, letter, email, social post, or in-person note — with or without a money demand
Frequency: The rarest integrity-event class in the product-safety estate: years can pass chain-wide without a credible episode; the sweep-decision discipline is exercised through the W627 mock-recall rotation
Volume: 1 event × the threat&#x27;s claimed scope (a single SKU, a category, one store, or the whole chain) × the sweep surface (targeted SKU pulls at ~200 stores, hours to a full-day campaign if ordered) × the notification set (PNP assessment, DTI-BPS/FDA per W2995 where consumers are at risk, the W2997 committee)
Owner: Product Safety &amp; Compliance Manager
Participants: Recall Committee chair (W2997), VP Legal (extortion/no-ransom posture), Store Operations leadership (sweep task campaigns), Loss Prevention (evidence and W1337 law-enforcement coordination), Corporate Communications (W3001-class customer-communication discipline), HSE Manager (VS-24), Category Manager (affected SKUs), PNP anti-cybercrime / economic-crime units
Source: workflow W5556 — Product-Tampering Threat, Extortion Demand &amp; Merchandise-Integrity Sweep Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5556_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5556_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5556_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5556_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5556_Lane2" name="VP Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5556_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5556_Lane3" name="Product Safety &amp; Compliance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5556_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5556_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5556_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5556_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5556_Lane4" name="Store Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5556_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5556_Lane5" name="Corporate Communications">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5556_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5556_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5556_Start7" name="A threat, extortion demand, or malicious claim that BuildRight merchandise on shelves has…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5556_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5556_Task8" name="Threat capture &amp; preservation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Threat capture &amp; preservation: verbatim record of every contact attempt; caller-line capture, envelope, email headers, and screenshots preserved in the case file; if the caller is live, keep them talking without negotiating
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Contact-center Agent / LP Duty
Accountable (A): Product Safety &amp; Compliance Manager
Duration: Immediate</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5556_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5556_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5556_Task9" name="Posture decision — never pay, never improvise public statements">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Posture decision — never pay, never improvise public statements: VP Legal with Product Safety confirm the no-payment rule and route all public communication through the W3001 discipline (no confirmation, no denial, no speculation outside scripted channels)
Responsible (R): VP Legal / Product Safety &amp; Compliance Manager
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Same day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5556_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5556_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5556_Task10" name="Credibility assessment with law enforcement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Credibility assessment with law enforcement: specificity of SKU/store/timing claimed, the claimant&#x27;s knowledge of real product detail, prior-contact history, and platform metadata assessed jointly with PNP; the assessment feeds and is filed with the sweep decision
Responsible (R): Product Safety &amp; Compliance Manager / LP Investigator
Accountable (A): Product Safety &amp; Compliance Manager
Duration: 4–24 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5556_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5556_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5556_Task11" name="Sweep-or-monitor decision (documented either way)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Sweep-or-monitor decision (documented either way): specific and credible → targeted sweep/quarantine of the named SKUs via W3000 stop-sale and quarantine at affected sites; vague or not credible → heightened monitoring and sample pulls only — the decision and its basis recorded on the case before execution
Responsible (R): Product Safety &amp; Compliance Manager / Recall Committee chair
Accountable (A): COO (chain-wide sweep only)
Duration: 4–24 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5556_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5556_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5556_Task12" name="Physical verification &amp; chain of custody">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Physical verification &amp; chain of custody: sample units pulled and inspected for seal/pack integrity; laboratory testing where contamination is chemically plausible; any altered unit found is preserved as evidence, never re-shelved or destroyed
Responsible (R): Store Operations / Quality / LP
Accountable (A): Product Safety &amp; Compliance Manager
Duration: 1–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5556_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5556_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5556_Task13" name="Regulatory posture">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Regulatory posture: W2995 DTI-BPS/FDA notification where a credible contamination risk to consumers exists; if altered product is verified, the W2994 recall decision runs on this evidence
Responsible (R): Product Safety &amp; Compliance Manager
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: Per W2995</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5556_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5556_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5556_Task14" name="Customer &amp; store communication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Customer &amp; store communication: scripted, no-speculation customer guidance per W3001 if a sweep is public-visible; store briefing pack so counter staff never improvise answers
Responsible (R): Corporate Communications / Store Operations
Accountable (A): Corporate Communications Director
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5556_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5556_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5556_Task15" name="Case file, hardening &amp; recurrence watch">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Case file, hardening &amp; recurrence watch: packaging/sealing review on tamper-prone SKUs, camera coverage review on affected aisles, threat intelligence filed to W1337, and the episode folded into the W627 mock rotation
Responsible (R): Product Safety &amp; Compliance Manager / LP
Accountable (A): Product Safety &amp; Compliance Manager
Duration: 2–6 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5556_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5556_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5556_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5556_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5556_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-496 (ensure controlled execution — Recall Initiation, Risk Assessment &amp; Regulatory Notification (PA-89.1).) | - operational: never-pay rule with VP Legal sign-off recorded on the case; sweep/stop-sale decision and its documented basis precede execution; altered units preserved under chain of custody, never re-shelved
Owner: Product Safety &amp; Compliance Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5556_Assoc18" sourceRef="W5556_Annotation17" targetRef="W5556_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5556_Flow19" sourceRef="W5556_Start7" targetRef="W5556_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W5556_Flow20" sourceRef="W5556_Task8" targetRef="W5556_Task9" />
